#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# appell_f2

#% text
# `appell_f2(a, b1, b2, c1, c2, x, y)` gives the Appell hypergeometric function `F2` of two variables.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# `F2 = sum (a)_(m+n) (b1)_m (b2)_n/((c1)_m (c2)_n m! n!) x^m y^n` for `|x| + |y| < 1` (DLMF 16.13.2).

#% item
# Numerical values: the sum over the rows of one variable of Gauss functions `hypergeometric_2f1` in the other (DLMF 16.13 summed over one index), the variable of smaller modulus outside; the inner Gauss function continues beyond the unit disk. Values are given where the row sum converges.

#% item
# At `x = 0` or `y = 0` the function is a Gauss function.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
appell_f2(3, 2, 1, 2, 3, 1/3, 0.2)
#% output
#= 4.821428571428571

#% cell
appell_f2(-2, -1, -2, 5, 2/3 + im, 0.4, 0.3)
#% output
#= 1.761819004524887 - 0.9741990950226244im

#% cell
n(appell_f2(3, 2, 1, 2, 3, 1/3, 2/5), 20)
#% output
#= 8.437500000000000000000

#% cell
appell_f2(im, 1, 1 + im, 3.2, 1/2, 0.5, 0.2 + 0.5*im)
#% output
#= 0.28690154267619583 - 0.5608139593449211im

#% cell
appell_f2(a, b1, b2, c1, c2, x, 0)
#% output
#= hypergeometric_2f1(a, b1, c1, x)

